# Finite horizontal quotients are p-groups

Theorem statement: `HorizontalPadicL.horizontalFiniteGroup_isPGroup_v2`
(`a0429464-ba69-45f9-8951-5b7ee90bba15`), by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25.

Proof: submission `471fd3be-558e-4955-a191-c8550a5088cb`, by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

Every finite horizontal quotient, being a finite product of additive groups Z/p^{m_i}Z, is a finite
p-group.

## Explanation of the source proof

The finite horizontal quotient is a finite product of additive cyclic groups of cardinality
$p^{m_i}$. Its cardinality is therefore

$$
\prod_i p^{m_i}=p^{\sum_i m_i}.
$$

The cardinality criterion for finite $p$-groups now gives the result.

